  9924	    - Each control must be a list.
  9925	  - **Now:** 95 tests, 56 mutants, all as predicted. The chain dry-run log has been refreshed under the new check.
  9926	- **Round 16 (Codex, `tools-review-codex-16.md`):** three more shapes got through the entry check:
  9927	  - a null first-day map, a null mapping entry, or a list used as a question id;
  9928	  - a split of two identical marks, which turned a lead into no winner in memory;
  9929	  - `company_figure: 1`.
  9930	
  9931	  This was the sixth round in a row with findings from one mechanism, so I stopped patching cases (AGENTS §1). The structural rule:
  9932	  `validate_readings` now walks the whole readings file top down, as one closed contract, and checks each container's type before
  9933	  reading it. Its docstring lists every shape, which is exactly what `mark_cards.readings` writes:
  9934	  - a split is two different marks;
  9935	  - flags are JSON booleans;
  9936	  - a mapping entry is exactly `{question, covers: true or "split"}`, naming a carded question;
  9937	  - the six draws are checked here (folded in from `verdict`);
  9938	  - the inputs are seven text fields.
  9939	
  9940	  It runs before `verify_inputs`, so neither can crash on a malformed file.
  9941	
  9942	  Results: 95 tests; 59 mutants, all as predicted (three stale ones repointed); the chain dry run passes the check.
  9943	- **Round 17 (Codex, `tools-review-codex-17.md`).** The contract allowed two things it should not have:
  9944	  - a missing first-day map, or a card missing `opened`, which silently dropped opening delays;
  9945	  - a named input path that is a directory, which crashed.
  9946	
  9947	  Fixed:
  9948	  - The contract now requires the full first-day map, keyed exactly by the listed matters, and every card's nullable `opened`. This is
  9949	    what `mark_cards.readings` always writes, and the chain dry run passes.
  9950	  - `verify_inputs` turns any failure to read a named file as its writer wrote it into a refusal.
  9951	
  9952	  Now at 96 tests and 62 mutants, all as predicted.
  9953	- **Round 18 (Codex, `tools-review-codex-18.md`):** a well-formed but edited readings file could flip a verdict. Codex turned one answered card into "no answer" and the verdict went from loss to lead. Changed opening and first-article days were also accepted. Separately, a draw that opened no question was refused instead of scored as too small, because the writer left out its card map.
  9954	  - **Structural rule, one owner:** the scorer no longer scores a readings file it is handed. `score_comparison.score(mapping out, marks folder)` builds the readings with their one writer, `mark_cards.build_readings`, from the named inputs, scores what it built, and refuses a `readings.json` that differs. The command line uses this entry, and so does the chain dry run.
  9955	  - **The deck key now decides two more card fields:** each card's answered flag and its opening day. Every draw keeps a card map, empty when the draw opened no question.
  9956	  - **Results:** 99 tests; 66 mutants, all as predicted; the chain dry run reaches its verdict through the new entry.
  9957	  - **Updated:** the step-4 command in CURRENT_STATE.
